# Learn more https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Native projects. This app uses Continuous Native Generation: android/ and
# ios/ are produced by `expo prebuild` from app.json and the config plugins,
# so they are build output, not source. The local android/ tree is over 1 GB.
#
# Nothing hand-written lives in there. The one thing that used to — the
# LiveKit/WebRTC ProGuard keep rules, without which R8 fails the release
# build — is now declared as `extraProguardRules` under expo-build-properties
# in app.json, so prebuild regenerates it. Do not edit android/ by hand; a
# change made there is lost at the next prebuild and is invisible to CI.
/android/
/ios/

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local env files (never commit real keys)
.env
.env*.local

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
